<html>
  <head>
    <title>Database Support Admin</title>
    <meta name="decorator" content="atl.admin">
    $webResourceManager.requireResource("com.keysight.database:database-admin-config-resources")
  </head>
  <body>

    <form id="database-admin-config" class="aui">

       <h2>Installed JDBC Drivers</h2>

       <p>In order to communicate with an external relational database system
       such as mysql, the jdbc drivers need to be provided.  For licensing reasons,
       these cannot be distributed with the plugin.  Please provide the directory
       where the driver .jar files will be found on the server hosting Confluence.
       Note, paths on windows should be specified as <b>C:\\JdbcDrivers</b> (with
       double slashes) while linux paths should look like <b>/JdbcDrivers</b>.  Paths
       may be absolute or relative.  If relative, they are relative to the directory
       <b>$relativeHome</b>.</p>

       <div class="config-input-continer">
          <div class="config-input-row">
             <div class="config-input-cell">
                <div class="field-group">
                    <label for="jdbc-driver-directory">Local Directory with JDBC Drivers</label>
                    <input class="text full-width-field" type="text" id="jdbc-driver-directory" name="jdbc-driver-directory" title="JDBC Driver Directory">
                    <div class="error add-group-error"></div>
                </div>
             </div>
             <div class="config-input-cell">
                <div class="field-group right-button">
                   <div class="buttons-container right-button">
                      <input id="save-jdbc-driver-directory" class="button submit" type="submit" value="Save">
                   </div>
                </div>
             </div>
          </div>
       </div>

       <div id="installed-drivers-container" class="list-container"></div>

       <hr />
       <div id="connection-profiles">
       </div>
       <input id="add-connection-profile" class="button submit" type="submit" value="Add Connection Profile">

    </form>
  </body>
</html>
